      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "Seriously cant wait. I cant stand SteamVR apps and their want for the game and monitor to be on the same card. Oculus does't really have that requirement. And I really REALLY dont want to invest another $100 for a new display that has Display 1.7 ports and then buy a $20 cable just to connect the two, I play plenty of games using oculus itsself that run fine seperated. My work around right now is a awkward one haha, Put my VR on my head above my eyes so I can see my monitor and attempt to play normally, its a difficult thing to do haha and awkward to!",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
