      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I imagine this 𝙢𝙖𝙮 no longer be much of a focus (if at all), especially if SteamVR seems to cause fewer issues. I personally would prefer less middle-man, but it is understandable. I have some issues inconsistencies that do pop up with no help or as a result of there being a OpenVR/SteamVR middle-man. Thankfully these don't ruin things so much. Opening my menu, Oculus or SteamVR is unpredictable in how it will affect frame-rate at this time in my experience. It, an unfortunate amount of the time, does bring my framerate down to a quarter or half of what I know my hardware is capable of pushing out and would have been just a click before. Random opening and closing of the SteamVR and Oculus menus sometimes fixes this; but more often than not it won't and I have to wait an extended period of time or restart VRChat (not SteamVR).\n\nJust sharing my experience, although better than it used to be.\nBy far.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
